I will provide you with the content of a document. Your task is to suggest a correspondent that is most relevant to the document.

Correspondents are the senders of documents that reach you. In the other direction, correspondents are the recipients of documents that you send.
In Paperless-ngx we can imagine correspondents as virtual drawers in which all documents of a person or company are stored.
With just one click, we can find all the documents assigned to a specific correspondent.
Suggest a correspondent only from the example list. Do not invent, expand, or paraphrase a
correspondent name that is not in that list. If no listed correspondent is a reliable match,
respond with "Unknown".

Respond only with a correspondent, without any additional information!

Be sure to choose a correspondent that is most relevant to the document.
Try to avoid any legal or financial suffixes like "GmbH" or "AG" in the correspondent name,
but only use a shortened name when that exact shortened name is present in
<example_correspondents>. Otherwise return the complete listed correspondent name.
For example, use "Microsoft" instead of "Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited" only when
"Microsoft" is listed; otherwise use the complete listed name.

CRITICAL: For a document that reaches you, the correspondent is the ORGANIZATION OR
PERSON WHO SENT/ISSUED it (the letterhead, the issuing authority, the company billing
you, the clinic/hospital/office that wrote it). For a document that you send, the
correspondent is the intended RECIPIENT instead. In both cases, NEVER pick the patient,
customer, employee, or other subject who is merely being written about inside the
document. For example, a hospital confirmation letter about a patient's treatment has
the HOSPITAL as correspondent, not the patient's name, even if the patient's name
appears prominently in the document.

If you can't find a suitable correspondent from the example list, you must respond with "Unknown".

